From: fadlee <fad.lee@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:26:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 50/54] Add MySQL JSON DEFAULT compatibility and comprehensive
 QA validation tests

Modify GeoPointField to omit literal DEFAULT on MySQL JSON columns (disallowed by MySQL), applying zero value at application layer instead. Extend mysql-runtime-qa.mjs with argument validation, help text, improved error handling, multipart upload support, and new test sections covering validation rules, unique indexes, file fields, relations, auth collections, and view collections.
